From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mobile-nav): drop the drawer's own close row and the
 ghost rail entries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- StudioNavigationRail: drop the group-chat / workflow / device-connections
  entries (their routes and views are removed by the fork) and point the chat
  entry at the existing sidebar.chat key instead of the removed
  sidebar.singleChat one, so a raw key is never rendered.
- MobileNavigationDrawer: the drawer's own 40px close row is gone (the page
  sidebar's own close button is the affordance again, un-suppressed).
- ChatPanel: tighten the mobile page-sidebar header paddings now that the ☰ no
  longer floats over it.

The 0.7.26 version of this patch also overrode the drawer's top safe-area inset
to a hardcoded 0 (the K60 shell then double-padded the content, which read as a
dead band). That override is dropped here: with the web-to-app shell running
fullscreen + persistent transparent status bar the window is truly edge-to-edge,
the shell reserves no top padding, and env(safe-area-inset-top) is the only
correct inset — overriding it buried the drawer's first row under the status
bar. The upstream inset lines stand as they are.
---
 .../src/components/hermes/chat/ChatPanel.vue  | 13 ++++++++++
 .../layout/MobileNavigationDrawer.vue         | 26 +++----------------
 .../layout/StudioNavigationRail.vue           |  8 ++----
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/ChatPanel.vue b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/ChatPanel.vue
index 33989ba7b..5ee26239c 100644
--- a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/ChatPanel.vue
+++ b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/ChatPanel.vue
@@ -3466,6 +3466,19 @@ function handleSessionModelSelect(selection: { model: string; provider: string }
   padding: calc(12px * var(--spacing-scale, 1));
 }
 
+@media (max-width: $breakpoint-mobile) {
+  // Inside the mobile drawer the ☰ no longer floats over the sidebar, so the
+  // vertical padding the old overlay design needed is dead space above the
+  // session list. Tighten it (and the first group header) instead.
+  .page-sidebar-top {
+    padding: 10px 12px 6px;
+  }
+
+  .session-group-header {
+    padding: 4px 10px 3px;
+  }
+}
+
 .page-sidebar-tabs {
   display: flex;
   flex-direction: column;
